<Figure src="/images/texdesk/editor-screenshot.jpg" alt="Screenshot of TeXdesk with a LaTeX file beside its PDF preview" caption="Lecture notes in TeXdesk, with the PDF building beside the source" />

TeXdesk is a lightweight LaTeX editor for macOS, for writing homework and notes directly in `.tex` files as fast as Markdown. Intended to be a Overleaf-Obsidian hybrid, for students, researchers, and anyone who writes latex. Every edited file builds locally in-place, so the file tree remains clean. A smart PDF viewer allows for easy page navigation.

TeXdesk has a typescript plugin engine for writing convenient shortcuts and functions that read editor context. Gille Castel's vim snippets are a built-in plugin. It also has customizable workspaces for folder overviews and templates defined in the app.

TeXdesk supports tikz graphics, with a built-in AI-powered diagram editor that understands page context and can quickly generate figures.
